---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProductPicks from '../../components/ProductPicks.astro';
import { guides } from '../../lib/guides';
const by = (slug: string) => guides.find((g) => g.slug === slug)!;
const sections: { h: string; blurb: string; slugs: string[] }[] = [
  { h: 'Holiday 2026', blurb: 'Black Friday is Friday, November 27, 2026, and Cyber Monday is Monday, November 30. These pages list what to have on hand — a spare cartridge, chemicals, a cover — and the USPS and UPS send-by dates. They do not print a price, a percent off, or a countdown.', slugs: ['black-friday-hot-tub-filter-and-spa-care','gifts-for-hot-tub-owners-2026','winter-spa-care'] },
  { h: 'Find the right cartridge', blurb: 'Start here when the number on the end cap is missing, two catalogs disagree, or the diameter matches and the filter still will not seal. These guides use the same fields the Unicel 2026 guide and the Pleatco 2023 catalog print: diameter, length, top, bottom and media area.', slugs: ['how-to-find-your-spa-filter-size','open-end-vs-threaded-hot-tub-filters','why-same-size-spa-filters-have-different-square-feet','oem-vs-unicel-vs-pleatco-spa-filters','how-filbur-unicel-and-pleatco-numbers-compare'] },
  { h: 'By spa brand', blurb: 'The part number on your old cartridge is still the best lookup. These guides explain the splits that a model name hides: Hot Spring collection sizes, Caldera slip versus open bottoms, Bullfrog thread length and coreless socks, Sundance and Jacuzzi look-alikes, Master Spas Eco-Pur, and Intex versus Bestway inflatable cartridges.', slugs: ['hot-spring-filter-sizes-by-collection','caldera-filter-bottom-fittings','bullfrog-threaded-and-coreless-filters','sundance-and-jacuzzi-look-alike-filters','master-spas-eco-pur-filters','intex-and-bestway-inflatable-spa-filters','spas-that-use-more-than-one-filter'] },
  { h: 'Clean, install and replace', blurb: 'Schedules and procedures from Hot Spring, Jacuzzi, Sundance, Unicel and Pleatco. A housing that holds two or three cartridges is a different count from the spare set those makers tell you to keep on the shelf.', slugs: ['how-to-clean-a-hot-tub-filter','how-often-to-clean-hot-tub-filter','how-to-install-a-hot-tub-filter','how-often-to-replace-hot-tub-filter','signs-your-hot-tub-filter-is-bad','clogged-or-missing-hot-tub-filter','hot-tub-flow-error-codes-and-your-filter','should-you-acid-wash-a-spa-filter','can-you-put-a-hot-tub-filter-in-the-dishwasher','spa-filter-cleaner-vs-diy-soak','best-hot-tub-filter-cleaners'] },
  { h: 'Water care and supplies', blurb: 'Test strips, sanitizer, shock, stains and the safety notes from CDC and CPSC. Full buying guides for covers, steps and tools live on the supplies hub.', slugs: ['best-hot-tub-test-strips','how-to-balance-hot-tub-ph-and-alkalinity','best-hot-tub-sanitizer-bromine-chlorine-mineral','hot-tub-shock-chlorine-vs-non-chlorine','hot-tub-foam-cloudy-water-and-jet-cleaners','hot-tub-stain-scale-and-metal-control','hot-tub-chemical-safety-and-storage','hot-tub-cover-lifters-and-cover-care','hot-tub-steps-handrails-and-safe-entry','hot-tub-cleaning-tools-skimmers-and-vacuums','replacement-hot-tub-headrests-and-pillows'] },
];
---
<Base title="Hot Tub Guides – Filters, Water Care, Covers & Supplies | MySpaFilter" description="Cited guides for hot tub filters and water care: sizes, fittings, Hot Spring, Caldera, Bullfrog, Sundance, Intex, cleaning, replacement and supplies.">
<p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Guides</p>
<h1>Hot tub guides</h1>
<p>These guides answer the questions that come up after you pull a cartridge out of a hot tub: which number to trust, why two filters with the same diameter are not the same part, how often to clean, and what a flow error is actually reporting. Every size, part number and safety statement is tied to a published source. The sources are manufacturer manuals and catalog pages (Unicel, Pleatco, Filbur, Hot Spring, Jacuzzi, Sundance, Intex, Bestway), dealer listings we name on the cartridge page, and CDC or CPSC pages where the topic is health or chemical safety. If a catalog does not give a number, the guide says the column is blank.</p>
<p>MySpaFilter’s main job is still the cross-reference. {guides.length} guides sit next to the cartridge table, not instead of it. When you already have a part number, <a href="/">search it</a> or use the <a href="/tools/cross-reference/">cross-reference lookup</a>, which lists every match on one page. When you only have a tape measure, use the <a href="/size/">size lookup</a> and the <a href="/guide/">measuring guide</a>, then come back here for the fitting and the brand splits. Published clean and replace intervals can be counted from a date on the <a href="/tools/filter-schedule/">replace and clean calculator</a>. The whole cited table, with CSV and JSON downloads, is the <a href="/data/">dataset</a>.</p>

<h2>How to use this hub</h2>
<p>Read the end cap first. An OEM number such as Hot Spring 71825, Caldera 1019401, Sundance 6540-488 or Intex 29001E beats a photo of “a spa filter.” The search box on the homepage accepts OEM, Unicel, Pleatco and Filbur numbers. The page you land on lists the equivalents, the diameter and length, the top and bottom fittings, and the document each figure came from. Retailer buttons on that page, including Amazon, use the part number. They are affiliate links, disclosed on the page and in the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
<p>Use a guide when the search result is ambiguous. That happens in a few repeating ways:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Same outside size, different ends.</strong> Caldera’s 7" × 10-3/4" cartridges include a 2" male slip bottom and a 2-11/16" open bottom. The <a href="/guides/open-end-vs-threaded-hot-tub-filters/">open-end versus threaded</a> guide and the <a href="/guides/caldera-filter-bottom-fittings/">Caldera bottoms</a> guide are the pair to read.</li>
<li><strong>Same OEM number, different detail.</strong> Sundance C-8326 and C-8327 share 6540-488 and a 125 sq ft body; Unicel splits them on a core plug. Jacuzzi OEM 373045 is printed on both a 25 sq ft and a 50 sq ft cartridge. See <a href="/guides/sundance-and-jacuzzi-look-alike-filters/">look-alike Sundance and Jacuzzi filters</a> and <a href="/guides/why-same-size-spa-filters-have-different-square-feet/">why square-foot ratings differ</a>.</li>
<li><strong>The brand changed the cartridge by year.</strong> Hot Spring Highlife, earlier Limelight and 2018-and-later Limelight are three different bodies. A 2014 Caldera Cantabria depends on the production quarter. Start with <a href="/guides/hot-spring-filter-sizes-by-collection/">Hot Spring sizes by collection</a> or the model-year lookups for <a href="/fitment/hot-spring-filter-by-model-year/">Hot Spring</a>, <a href="/fitment/caldera-filter-by-model-year/">Caldera</a>, <a href="/fitment/jacuzzi-filter-by-model-year/">Jacuzzi</a>, <a href="/fitment/sundance-filter-by-model-year/">Sundance</a>, <a href="/fitment/bullfrog-filter-by-model-year/">Bullfrog</a> and <a href="/fitment/master-spas-filter-by-model-year/">Master Spas</a>.</li>
<li><strong>More than one cartridge in the well.</strong> Some Hot Spring listings call for three of the 6" cartridge. Unicel says later Master Spas Eco-Pur systems require two outer cartridges plus an inner element. Sundance pairs a pleated filter with a disposable insert. <a href="/guides/spas-that-use-more-than-one-filter/">Spas that use more than one filter</a> separates that from a spare set on the shelf.</li>
<li><strong>An inflatable spa.</strong> Intex Type S1 and Type S2 are different cartridges, and the letters on the set number decide which list you are on. Bestway Type VI is a third size, with a Monte Carlo exception. See <a href="/guides/intex-and-bestway-inflatable-spa-filters/">Intex and Bestway filters</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Brand tables are the index behind those guides: <a href="/hot-spring/">Hot Spring</a>, <a href="/caldera/">Caldera</a>, <a href="/bullfrog/">Bullfrog</a>, <a href="/sundance/">Sundance</a>, <a href="/jacuzzi/">Jacuzzi</a>, <a href="/master-spas/">Master Spas</a>, <a href="/intex/">Intex</a>, <a href="/bestway/">Bestway</a>. Each brand page links the guides that apply to it and includes Amazon searches for part numbers from that table.</p>

<h2>What we will not put in a guide</h2>
<p>We do not invent a part number to fill a blank column, and we do not average two catalogs when they print different lengths or different square-foot ratings. Softub OEM 90-802 is the clear example: Unicel and Filbur rate it at 25 sq ft and Pleatco rates it at 20, while the size and the thread agree. The guide says both. We also do not publish prices or star ratings. Product links are either a listing whose title we opened and checked, or an Amazon search for the part number. The tag on those links is this site’s Associates tag. Commissions do not change a cross-reference row. The <a href="/about/#methodology">methodology and corrections policy</a> explain how to report a number that does not match your cartridge. The byline on every guide is the MySpaFilter Editorial Team.</p>
<p>Cleaning and replacement copy is limited to what the cited manual says. Hot Spring, Jacuzzi and Sundance do not all use one interval, and the guides keep the differences. Flow-error codes depend on who made the control system (Gecko, Balboa, Sundance, Hot Spring), so the <a href="/guides/hot-tub-flow-error-codes-and-your-filter/">flow-error guide</a> names the code and the document, and <a href="/guides/clogged-or-missing-hot-tub-filter/">clogged or missing filters</a> explains why the manuals say not to run the spa with the cartridge out.</p>
<p>Water-care guides are grouped on <a href="/supplies/">hot tub supplies</a>. They cite CDC and Hot Spring ranges and then list products. They are not a substitute for the owner’s manual, which is also what the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> says.</p>

{sections.map((s) => (
  <section><h2>{s.h}</h2><p>{s.blurb}</p>
  <ul class="grid">{s.slugs.map((slug) => { const g = by(slug); return <li class="card"><a href={`/guides/${g.slug}/`} style="font-weight:750;font-size:1.08rem">{g.title}</a><p class="crumbs">{g.desc}</p></li>; })}</ul></section>
))}
<ProductPicks heading="Search a part number on Amazon" lead="If you already know the number, these searches open Amazon for that part. If you do not, use the homepage search and the retailer buttons on the cartridge page." groups={[{h:'Common part-number searches', search:[
  ['Hot Spring 71825 / C-6430','71825 spa filter','6" × 10-1/2" open-end cartridge. Some models take three.'],
  ['Caldera 73531 / C-7375','73531 spa filter','7" × 14-3/4" open-bottom cartridge.'],
  ['Unicel C-4950','C-4950 spa filter','4-15/16" × 13-5/16" open-end cartridge.'],
  ['Intex 29001E','Intex 29001E Type S1','PureSpa Type S1. Not the S2 cartridge.'],
]}]} />
<p>Something in a guide that the source does not support? Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. The only address we publish is contact@myspafilter.com.</p>
</Base>
